  "finalText": "BRCA1's reviewed UniProtKB accession is P38398, and the EBI Proteins API coordinates for it put the gene on chromosome 17 with Ensembl gene ID ENSG00000012048.\n\n1. **Accession:** A UniProtKB search for the exact gene name BRCA1, limited to human (taxon 9606) and reviewed entries, returned one Swiss-Prot entry, P38398 (BRCA1_HUMAN).\n2. **Coordinates:** The coordinates response for P38398 was too large to display in full, so I read the two fields with the tool's built-in checks. The checks report the actual value at a given location in the response:\n   - `gnCoordinate[0].genomicLocation.chromosome` = **\"17\"**\n   - `gnCoordinate[0].ensemblGeneId` = **\"ENSG00000012048\"**\n\nBoth values come from the first coordinate record in the response. I couldn't view the rest of the response, so I didn't check whether every other record says the same.\n\nANSWER: P38398 | 17 | ENSG00000012048"
